{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{% set output_format_description = "a brief, objective observation (2-3 sentences) focused solely on the primary trend or key finding from the 'Distribution of Attack Vectors' chart data. No interpretation or recommendations." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
The chart titled '{{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Distribution of Attack Vectors') }}' displays the overall count or percentage of CVEs for each primary attack vector type (e.g., Network, Local, Physical, Adjacent).
Examine the provided data summary for this chart.
Identify and describe the most significant observation. For example:
- Which attack vector is most prevalent?
- Are there any attack vectors that are significantly less common?
- What is the general distribution across different vector types?
Focus only on what the data directly indicates regarding the distribution of attack vectors.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Chart ID: {{ data_context_payload.chart_id | default('overall_attack_vector_dist') }}
Chart Caption: {{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Figure 4. Distribution of Attack Vectors.') }}

Data Summary:
{{ data_context_payload.chart_data_summary | default("Data not available.") }}
Note: If percentages do not sum to 100%, this may be due to some CVEs lacking an assigned value (i.e., missing or NaN values were excluded from the calculation).
{% endblock data_context %}
